    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "The Earth's lithosphere is divided into major and minor tectonic plates that float on the ductile asthenosphere.",
        "Mantle convection currents driven by interior thermal heat are the primary force moving tectonic plates.",
        "Tectonic plate interactions occur along three main boundary types: Convergent, Divergent, and Transform.",
        "Major plates include the Pacific, North American, South American, Eurasian, African, Indo-Australian, and Antarctic plates.",
        "Plate tectonics explains major geological features including fold mountains, ocean trenches, mid-ocean ridges, and volcanic arcs."
      ],
      "id": "5pe6zh1"
