    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Remember boundary classifications: Convergent margins are Destructive, Divergent margins are Constructive, and Transform margins are Conservative.",
        "Mid-Oceanic Ridges (e.g., Mid-Atlantic Ridge) are formed at Divergent boundaries, whereas deep-sea trenches (e.g., Mariana Trench) form at Convergent boundaries.",
        "The San Andreas Fault is a classic exam example of a Transform fault boundary characterized by strike-slip motion."
      ],
